# Trusted edge certificate-authority (CA) public keys: one OpenSSH public-key
# line per CA. Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#
# Edges authenticate with a USER certificate signed by one of these CAs; the
# gateway trusts the CA, not individual edge keys. An edge's clientId is its SSH
# username, which must be one of the certificate's principals.
#
# Create a CA and sign an edge certificate:
#   ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f ca_key                 # the CA keypair (keep ca_key secret)
#   ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f edge_clientA           # the edge's own keypair
#   ssh-keygen -s ca_key -I clientA -n clientA \     # -I keyId (audit), -n principal (= clientId)
#              -V +1h edge_clientA.pub               # -V validity window
# then put the CA *public* key below:
#
# ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...CA-public-key... ca@example.com
#
# Copy this file to config/trusted_user_ca (gitignored) and add your CA key(s).
